  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Strangler Fig at the edge",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "html",
        "content": "\n<div style=\"font-family: monospace; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<b>CLIENT</b> (frontend, tests, curl) &nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp; <b>KONG :8088</b> &nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp; decides per <b>PATH + METHOD</b><br/>\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&#9500;&#9472;&#9472; <b>/users</b> &nbsp;GET &rarr; <i>panel below</i> &nbsp;|&nbsp; POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE &rarr; <i>panel below</i><br/>\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&#9492;&#9472;&#9472; <b>/sales</b> &nbsp;GET &rarr; <i>panel below</i> &nbsp;|&nbsp; POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE &rarr; <i>panel below</i><br/>\n<span style=\"opacity:0.7\">The client URL never changes. Switch: <code>.\\scripts\\route-users-to-service.ps1</code> &middot; rollback: <code>.\\scripts\\route-users-to-monolith.ps1</code>.\nThe monolith stays the SOURCE OF TRUTH: writes go to a microservice only after an explicit, acknowledged write cutover.</span>\n</div>\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "/users  READS (GET)",
      "description": "Where Kong route 'users-read' points RIGHT NOW (configured state from the Admin API via gateway-route-exporter - valid even with zero traffic).",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "max(gateway_route_on_monolith{route=\"users-read\"})",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
